KernelSU (kernel-side driver) — vendored snapshot

  source   : https://github.com/backslashxx/KernelSU
  branch   : master
  commit   : 709711bd91f2c9098bd35dc9036291ba8863a276 ("KernelSU v3.3.1+")
  upstream commit date : 2026-08-17
  vendored on          : 2026-10-22

  layout   : only KernelSU/kernel/ is vendored (the kernel driver);
             manager/userspace are not needed to build the kernel.

  wiring (mirrors upstream kernel/setup.sh):
    drivers/kernelsu -> ../KernelSU/kernel        (symlink)
    drivers/Makefile : obj-$(CONFIG_KSU) += kernelsu/
    drivers/Kconfig  : source "drivers/kernelsu/Kconfig"

  hook mode for this 4.14 non-GKI tree:
    CONFIG_KSU=y
    CONFIG_KSU_TAMPER_SYSCALL_TABLE=y   (sys_call_table hijack for sucompat +
                                         sys_reboot; no kprobes, no manual
                                         fs/*.c hooks; upstream recommends
                                         this mode for 3.0 - 4.14)

## SuSFS integration (added on top of vendor snapshot)

- fs/susfs.c + include/linux/susfs{,_def}.h: SuSFS v2.3.0 ported from
  crDroid xiaomi sm8150 (branch 16.0, susfs4ksu-next line) -- the only
  live 4.14-class reference carrying v2.3.0 with backslashxx-style KSU.
- 18 kernel hook sites wired (namei, readdir, open, namespace, statfs,
  stat, super, proc/{base,cmdline,fd,task_mmu}, proc_namespace, shmem,
  memory, kallsyms, sys, avc) adapted to CAF/MSM 4.14.357 divergences
  (legacy mnt_id ida, task_mmu show_map_vma is_pid arg, MSM stat, etc).
- KSU glue mirrors crDroid reference: ksu.c susfs_init, supercall
  SUSFS_MAGIC routing (MEMFD double-return bug fixed), dispatch
  boot monitor + MARK_GET variant, setuid_hook susfs umount gating
  (adapted to cred-based ksu_handle_setresuid_cred; task_work leak in
  crDroid's ksu_handle_extra_susfs_work fixed), kernel_umount
  try_umount exported, selinux.{c,h} sid helpers, rules.c sid capture,
  Kconfig "KernelSU - SUSFS" menu, Makefile SUSFS_VERSION banner.
- defconfig: CONFIG_KSU_SUSFS=y + all features except SUS_MEMFD.
- uapi/: backslashxx KernelSU root uapi headers (for custom manager
  builds; stock APK v3.3.1+22 needs nothing from here).
